{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm the force-exit grace accounts for the worst-case number of _GIT_TIMEOUT-bounded git children a single locked stage_and_commit can run, not just one.","criteria":["correctness","edge-cases"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["config.py:95: `return float(_lock._DEFAULT_TIMEOUT * _lock._DEFAULT_ATTEMPTS + _GIT_TIMEOUT)` — single _GIT_TIMEOUT term","event_append.py:167-208: a single locked stage_and_commit runs `_git_add`, then `_git_commit`, then on failure `_recover_from_unmerged`/`_recover_from_invalid_object`/`_unstage` — each a separate _run_git child bounded by _GIT_TIMEOUT","event_commit_git.py:43-44 comment: 'a stalled volume holds the lock up to this bound per call' — acknowledges per-call, but the grace counts only one call"],"finding":"The force-exit grace budgets only a single _GIT_TIMEOUT (shutdown_force_exit_grace_seconds = lock_budget + _GIT_TIMEOUT), but one stage_and_commit holds the write lock across multiple bounded git children (add, commit, and on failure recovery reads/unstage), each bounded at 120s. A stalled volume can thus hold the lock for several multiples of _GIT_TIMEOUT, so force-exit can still fire mid-write and orphan the mkdir lock — the exact outcome the grace is meant to prevent. Raising the bound 30->120 quadruples this unaccounted window.","id":"0","impact":0.45,"location":"src/rebar/review_bot/config.py:95","norm_id":"ncb434347e713a8d2","priority":0.45,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_acc